WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:29.120
Human Papilloma viruses, also called HPVs,
make up a group of over 100 related viruses

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.970
that infect people.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.900
Most HPVs can cause common skin warts, usually
on the hands or feet.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.370
However, about 40 types of HPV affect the
genitals, which are the sex organs on the

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.120
outside of the body.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.250
These HPVs cause the most common sexually
transmitted infections, illnesses transmitted

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:55.949
from one person to another through sexual
activity.

00:00:55.949 --> 00:01:02.290
Some genital HPVs are low-risk and may only
cause warts on and around the genitals and

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.420
anus of both women and men.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:12.890
Rarely, these HPVs can also cause warts inside
the mouth and throat.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.740
Other genital HPVs are high-risk.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:22.180
They can lead to cancer of the lower end of
the woman’s uterus called the cervix.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:28.400
Less commonly, these HPVs can lead to other
genital, oral, or anal cancers in both women

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.400
and men.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:35.470
It’s important to know that most HPV infections
cause no symptoms and the low-risk genital

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:43.610
HPVs that cause warts are not an important
cause of cancer.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:49.780
People infected with either a high-risk or
low-risk genital HPV spread it through skin-to-skin

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:55.090
contact during vaginal, oral, or anal sex.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:01.370
For infection to occur, HPV enters through
tiny cuts in the skin around or inside the

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:07.810
penis, vagina, throat, or anus.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:14.300
The virus makes it way down to the cells in
the bottom or basal layer of skin and infects

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.780
them.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:21.030
As the infected cells divide, the virus begins
to make copies of itself.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:27.370
Eventually, the infected cells move up through
the skin layers, releasing new viruses that

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:32.000
can spread the infection to other cells.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.159
For most people, the cells of the immune system
can destroy the infected cells along with

00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:44.450
the virus within two years, but in some people,
the immune system isn’t able to destroy

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:51.170
all the viruses, leading to an infection that
doesn’t go away.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:58.510
HPV-infected cells may multiply over several
weeks or months.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:06.510
If the cells are infected with low-risk HPV,
they begin to form warts around the genitals.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:12.060
If the HPV is high-risk, it may damage the
cells’ genetic material, causing the cells

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.749
to become precancerous.

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:20.389
Over a period of years, a cancerous tumor
may slowly form as the damaged cells continue

00:03:20.389 --> 00:03:24.819
to multiply.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:32.760
The most common cancer from high-risk genital
HPV is cervical cancer.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:40.359
There is no cure for any type of HPV infection;
however, the Gardasil vaccine can help protect

00:03:40.359 --> 00:03:46.239
against two of the most common high-risk HPVs
that cause genital cancers.

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:51.099
The vaccine also helps protect against two
of the most common low-risk HPVs that cause

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:55.010
genital warts.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:04:00.150
For best protection, pre-teen girls and boys
should receive three doses of the vaccine

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:07.269
over a period of six-months before any sexual
activity takes place.

00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:12.370
The vaccine injects dead proteins from HPV
viruses into the bloodstream.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:20.660
These proteins don’t cause infection, but
the proteins do stimulate certain immune cells

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:27.520
to create markers called antibodies that can
identify these HPVs.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:36.930
Later, if the live version of these viruses
invade the skin, these antibodies recognize

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:42.460
and attach to them.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:48.879
These immune cells destroy the marked viruses,
which prevents an infection from happening.

00:04:48.879 --> 00:04:54.610
It is important to note that the vaccine does
not protect against other types of HPV not

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.449
included in the vaccine.

00:04:56.449 --> 00:05:05.000
The vaccine also doesn’t reliably treat
cells that are already infected.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:12.580
High-risk genital HPVs that cause cervical
cancer are most treatable when diagnosed early.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.590
Women should have a PAP test to see if their
cervix has abnormal or precancerous cells

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:20.850
even if they’ve had a HPV vaccine.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:26.340
Check with a healthcare provider to find out
how often to get this test.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.720
During this procedure, a healthcare professional
will collect a small sample of cells from

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.659
the cervix.

00:05:34.659 --> 00:05:41.810
These cells will be examined under a microscope
to see if they’re abnormal or cancerous.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:47.810
A separate HPV test will look for genetic
material from high-risk types of HPV.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:53.740
When a PAP test and HPV test are done together,
it’s called contesting.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.449
If these tests show abnormal cells, a healthcare
provider will recommend specific treatment

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:06.020
based on the woman’s age, medical history,
and the abnormality of her cells.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:16.379
While there is no cure for an HPV infection,
both abnormal and cancerous cells can be treated.

00:06:16.379 --> 00:06:22.460
Some types of HPV can cause common skin warts
or genital warts.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:28.009
The warts may go away without treatment as
the immune system fights off the HPV infection.

00:06:28.009 --> 00:06:33.340
If the warts are painful or don’t go away,
visit a healthcare provider, so they can examine

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.990
the warts to determine the best way to remove
them.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:44.160
Although you can treat common warts at home,
do not treat genital warts yourself.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:53.330
Procedures to remove either common warts or
genital warts include freezing with cryotherapy,

00:06:53.330 --> 00:07:04.650
burning with an electric current called electrocautery,
or by surgical removal.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.219
For more information, talk to a healthcare
professional.

